# Required skills
Required skills: poteto-mode,tdd
The request named these skills, so each one must shape this work, and firstmate checks the record mechanically.
1. Before any other status line, load each skill (`/poteto-mode`, `/tdd`) through the skill tool or read its complete SKILL.md, then report one start proof per skill: `working [at=<epoch>]: skill-start <name> path=<SKILL.md path you read> route=<your first routing decision under it>`
   Firstmate leaves a start-proof record in your steering inbox and keeps ringing it until every start proof is present, even after you acknowledge it.
2. Before reporting done, report one line per skill saying how it shaped the work: `working [at=<epoch>]: skill-shaped <name>: <how the skill shaped the work>`
   A done without one is refused, naming the missing skill.

# Definition of done
Write your findings to `{run-worktree}/.test-required-skills/parent/data/skill-scout/report.md`.
The report must stand alone: what you did, what you found, the evidence (commands run, output, file:line references), and what you recommend.
Lavish is unavailable (lavish-axi is missing or below its supported version floor), so deliver your findings as a text report without Lavish, even for a visual deliverable.
Before reporting done, read and follow `{run-worktree}/.agents/skills/captain-hold-lifecycle/SKILL.md` and pass its shared completion gate for the report and any visual review.
Only when the reviewed inventory is empty, run `FM_HOME='{run-worktree}/.test-required-skills/parent' bash '{run-worktree}/bin/fm-captain-hold.sh' complete 'skill-scout' --none`.
This exception permits only that command, not direct metadata edits, another task, or any backlog write.
If any captain call remains, ask firstmate to register the inventory and attest completion before you report done.
If the command refuses, report the refusal to firstmate and stop rather than bypassing the completion gate.
When the report is complete, append `done [at=<epoch>]: {one-line conclusion}` to the status file and stop.
If your findings reveal work that should ship (e.g. you reproduced a bug and the fix is clear), say so in the report; firstmate may promote this task in place, and you would then receive mode-specific ship instructions as a follow-up message.
